   "txt": "**1. Most Important Fact**\nInfosys has appointed Mitrankur Majumdar as Segment Head for Services Utilities Resources and Energy (\u2018SURE\u2019) and Senior Management Personnel effective August 24, 2026, as the current Segment Head, Ashiss Kumar Dash, transitions to focus on training and transition activities as CEO designate.\n\n**2. Key Numbers**\n* No financial metrics (revenue, EBITDA, margins, PAT) are stated in this filing.\n\n**3. Management Guidance / Forward-Looking Statements**\n* None provided in the document.\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**\n* No shareholder action required. Watch the leadership transition and operational continuity in the SURE business segment, as well as broader updates regarding Ashiss Kumar Dash's transition into the CEO role.\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**\n* **Neutral**: Standard internal leadership elevation to facilitate an orderly executive/CEO succession process."
  },
  {
   "s": "TCS",
   "n": "Tata Consultancy Services Limited",
   "cat": "Acquisition",
   "when": "2026-08-24 16:55",
   "sent": "positive",
   "txt": "Here is the equity-research summary of the regulatory filing:\n\n### 1. Most Important Fact\n**Tata Consultancy Services (TCS)**, through its wholly owned subsidiary Tata Consultancy Services Netherlands B.V., has approved the **100% acquisition of MHP Management- und IT-Beratung GmbH (\u201cMHP\u201d)**, an automotive and industrial consulting subsidiary of **Porsche AG**, coupled with a **\u20ac1.25 billion, 5-year strategic partnership deal** signed with Porsche.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated\n* **Acquisition Enterprise Value:** **\u20ac320 million** (cash consideration, excluding customary post-closing adjustments for net debt and working capital).\n* **Strategic Deal Size:** **\u20ac1.25 billion** over **5 years** with Porsche AG.\n* **Target Entity (MHP) Turnover:**\n  * **CY25:** \u20ac742 million\n  * **CY24:** \u20ac830 million\n  * **CY23:** \u20ac828 million\n* **Target Entity Headcount:** ~4,500 employees.\n* **TCS Reference Size:** Consolidated revenues of over **US $30 billion** for the fiscal year ended March 31, 2026.\n*(Note: EBITDA, margins, and PAT for the target are not disclosed in the document).*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Management Guidance & Forward Statements\n* **Deal Timeline:** Expected to close within **3\u20134 months**, subject to regulatory approvals (European Commission merger control, EU Foreign Subsidies Regulation, Romanian FDI clearance, and non-objection certificate from Germany's Federal Ministry of Economy and Energy).\n* **Strategic Intent:** \n  * TCS will establish a dedicated **AI Mobility Centre of Excellence (CoE)** to industrialize AI across Porsche's engineering, manufacturing, operations, and customer experience.\n  * TCS CEO K. Krithivasan stated the partnership aims to *\"industrialize AI at scale for Porsche, accelerating innovation across the value chain to deliver intelligent, software-defined mobility experiences of the future.\"*\n  * TCS has an overarching aspiration to become the *\"world's largest AI-led technology services company.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 4. What a Shareholder Should Watch / Act On\n* **Regulatory Clearances:** Monitor the receipt of required antitrust and foreign investment approvals in the EU, Germany, and Romania over the next 3\u20134 months.\n* **Integration & Revenue Accretion:** Track integration of ~4,500 consultants and revenue contribution (~\u20ac740M+ annual run rate) alongside execution milestones of the \u20ac1.25 billion 5-year Porsche contract.\n\n---\n\n### 5. One-Line Net Read\n**Positive**: Secures a substantial multi-year deal (\u20ac1.25B) with a marquee automotive client (Porsche) while adding deep European automotive and industrial consulting capabilities at an attractive valuation (~0.43x EV/CY25 Sales)."
  },
