   "txt": "Here is a concise summary based strictly on the provided regulatory filing:\n\n### 1. Most Important Fact\nL&T Energy Hydrocarbon Onshore (LTEH Onshore) has signed a contract for an **\"ultra-mega\" gas compression facilities project** for a client in the Middle East (against a Letter of Award issued in FY26), alongside two 230 kV extra-high-voltage substations to be executed by L&T\u2019s Power Transmission & Distribution business.\n\n### 2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated\n* **Order Value / Classification:** Categorized as **\"Ultra-Mega\"**, which per L&T's classification corresponds to a value **> \u20b915,000 Crore**.\n* **Substation Scope:** Execution of **two 230 kV** extra-high-voltage substations.\n* *Note: Specific revenue, EBITDA, margin, PAT, or exact contract value details beyond the classification range were not disclosed in the document.*\n\n### 3. Management Guidance / Outlook / Forward Statements\n* **E S Sathyanarayanan (SVP & Head of LTEH Onshore):** \n  > *\"The contract marks the start of a strategically important project that will add significant gas compression capacity and utility infrastructure. The project draws on our extensive experience in executing large and complex hydrocarbon facilities and reinforces our capability to deliver integrated solutions for challenging sour gas applications.\"*\n\n### 4. What a Shareholder Should Watch\n* Timely execution and margin delivery on this large-scale international EPC contract involving sour gas processing.\n* Formal revenue conversion and execution milestones flowing into the Energy Hydrocarbon segment order book.\n\n### 5. One-Line Net Read\n**Positive**, as signing a mega-scale contract (> \u20b915,000 Cr) significantly strengthens L&T's international order book and revenue visibility in the hydrocarbon sector."
